    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent lineup headlined by **Junior Caminero**, who commands an elite score of 81.92. His favorable matchup against Baz, combined with significant park factors, makes him our clear offensive anchor. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (66.51) and **Caleb Durbin** (68.37) are also priority starts; the Zebras' strategy of prioritizing speed is reflected in the boost granted to **Pete Crow-Armstrong** due to the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a high-probability environment for a stolen base. Meanwhile, **Kyle Schwarber** (63.83) and **Trea Turner** (62.21) maintain high utility as leadoff and top-order catalysts, despite facing an arm in Leahy that requires careful monitoring. **Christian Yelich** remains a strong play (64.82) due to a robust dynamic platoon advantage, which helps mitigate the modest matchup against Mahle.\n\nWe are exercising caution with **Yordan Alvarez** (53.21) and **Carson Benge** (44.55), both of whom face left-handed pitching that suppresses their ceiling; while they remain in the starting nine to maintain our category footprint, their scores sit well below our top-tier targets. **Chase Meidroth** was the most difficult bench decision, narrowly missing the cut with a score of 38.20. While **Chase Meidroth** offered moderate potential, he failed to cross our 40.0 \"Below Floor\" threshold, largely due to a subpar SP skill matchup against McLean that neutralized his base projections. We continue to hold **Gary Sanchez**, **Colt Keith**, and **Lars Nootbaar** in reserve; none are currently penciled into their respective MLB starting lineups, and they remain benched to conserve our precious game caps. We will continue to monitor the status of **Casey Schmitt**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Josh Smith**, **Jacob Gonzalez**, **Hector Rodriguez**, **Luis Pena**, and **Pedro Ramirez** as potential depth options should our starters face late-scratch scenarios or weather-related delays.",
